bettiTablesWithHilbertFunction -- list or tally all Betti tables that can be obtained from monomial ideals with a particular (partial or complete) Hilbert function
*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        bettiTablesWithHilbertFunction(L, R)
        bettiTablesWithHilbertFunction(L, R, BoundGenerators => a)
        bettiTablesWithHilbertFunction(L, R, FirstBetti => b)
        bettiTablesWithHilbertFunction(L, R, GradedBettis => B)
        bettiTablesWithHilbertFunction(L, R, SquareFree => x)
        bettiTablesWithHilbertFunction(L, R, Count => y)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, $\{h(0), h(1), \ldots, h(d)\}$,
        the values of a valid Hilbert function for $R$ for degrees $0\ldots d$.
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * BoundGenerators => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value
        -1, a degree bound on the monomial generators
      * FirstBetti => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null,
        a specified first total Betti number
      * GradedBettis => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value null,
        if the form $\{b_0, b_1, \ldots, b_d\}$, where $b_i$ is the first
        graded Betti numbers with degree $i$.
      * SquareFree => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether or not to consider squarefree monomial ideals only
      * Count => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, whether or not to return the count of unique tables instead of
        all values
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, all unique Betti tables that can be
        obtained from monomial ideals of $R$ with Hilbert function beginning
        with $L$, or
      * a *note tally: (Macaulay2Doc)Tally,, the same set of Betti tables, with
        the number of unique monomial ideals producing each one

Description
===========

This function calls *note monomialIdealsWithHilbertFunction:
monomialIdealsWithHilbertFunction, with the specified options, determines the
Betti table of each feasible monomial ideal, then lists or tallies the Betti
tables encountered. The Count option does not fundamentally change how the
computation is performed, only how the results are reported.

