minimalPrimesIP -- one line description if different from minimalPrimesIP
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        minimalPrimesIP I
        minimalPrimesIP (I, iterations)
  * Inputs:
      * I, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, 
      * iterations, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, how many iterations of
        topMinimalPrimesIP should be called
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the minimal primes of I

Description
===========

This is basically an alternative version of *note minimalPrimes:
(MinimalPrimes)minimalPrimes,.

This function calls *note topMinimalPrimesIP: topMinimalPrimesIP, repeatedly,
collecting the primes and passing them in with *note IgnorePrimes:
IgnorePrimes,. This is repeated iterations many times or until there are no
primes remaining. If iterations is excluded, all minimal primes are returned.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z,w,v];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal(y^12, x*y^3, z*w^3, z*v*y^10, z*x^10, v*z^10, w*v^10, |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R                                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|y*v*x*z*w);                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : ScipPrintLevel = 0;                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : minimalPrimesIP(I, 1)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {monomialIdeal (y, z, v), monomialIdeal (y, z, w)}                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : minimalPrimesIP I                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {monomialIdeal (y, z, v), monomialIdeal (y, z, w), monomialIdeal (x, y, |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     w, v)}                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : minimalPrimes I                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {monomialIdeal (y, z, w), monomialIdeal (y, z, v), monomialIdeal (x, y, |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     w, v)}                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Warning: more than likely, this with take longer than *note minimalPrimes:
(MinimalPrimes)minimalPrimes, to return the same output. It some situations
*note topMinimalPrimesIP: topMinimalPrimesIP, is much faster than *note
minimalPrimes: (MinimalPrimes)minimalPrimes,, but not all.

See also
========

  * *note minimalPrimes: (MinimalPrimes)minimalPrimes, -- minimal primes of an
    ideal
  * *note topMinimalPrimesIP: topMinimalPrimesIP, -- compute the minimal primes
    of maximum dimension using integer programming
  * *note IgnorePrimes: IgnorePrimes, -- Ignores certain primes when computing
    top minimal primes.

Ways to use minimalPrimesIP:
============================

  * "minimalPrimesIP(MonomialIdeal)"
  * "minimalPrimesIP(MonomialIdeal,ZZ)"

